From 56e75c889091ee1287476a74a442c1a626e2a55a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Barre <ludovic.barre@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Oct 2024 15:29:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1416/1695] product/tfm-stm32mp2: add firewall support in power
 domain

Add firewall support to set gpu power domain which access
to clocks (pll3, gpu) and regulator PWR_CR12.

errata 2 3 5:
Once the compartment filtering is enabled, the registers are
not writeable by any CIDs even the permitted one.

Workaround:
CID filtering should be disabled before accessing:
- PWR_CR12 (regulator)
- gpu clock.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a4c187a44f7f0c477274a07ad59179a51a6571ca product/tfm-stm32mp2: add firewall support in power domain]
Change-Id: If89799f41ea783c3c8efdbd039b37577c727d76f
Signed-off-by: Ludovic Barre <ludovic.barre@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/SCP-firmware/+/415066
Domain-Review: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
